WEBVTT

00:00:22.163 --> 00:00:24.688
W-What is that?

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:50.859
In my younger days, I lost

00:00:50.859 --> 00:00:56.731
even the reason for this pain

00:00:56.731 --> 00:01:02.437
Crouching over, making excuses

00:01:02.437 --> 00:01:05.634
I must have...

00:01:07.042 --> 00:01:13.315
Taking hold of the premonition
I saw at the end of the blue,

00:01:13.315 --> 00:01:20.922
riding the wind, I'm off
to where the light shines

00:01:20.922 --> 00:01:23.792
I'll always be with you

00:01:23.792 --> 00:01:26.294
see the sky in front of you

00:01:26.294 --> 00:01:30.663
fly high in a light from the deepest blue

00:01:32.467 --> 00:01:38.006
Riding the echo of swirling stars,

00:01:38.006 --> 00:01:40.675
I sing out

00:01:40.675 --> 00:01:49.344
May my voice reach you

00:02:02.297 --> 00:02:04.322
I won't let you touch Jin!

00:02:07.135 --> 00:02:08.762
Toa...

00:02:27.288 --> 00:02:31.292
Toa, who exactly are you?

00:02:31.292 --> 00:02:34.489
Please, close your eyes.

00:03:00.321 --> 00:03:01.982
Toa...

00:03:05.226 --> 00:03:07.990
Damn, I'm late.

00:03:09.597 --> 00:03:11.032
Is that?

00:03:11.032 --> 00:03:13.568
A new Dragon has incarnated
at the first observation platform

00:03:13.568 --> 00:03:15.603
on Shin-Ogasawara Bridge!

00:03:15.603 --> 00:03:18.333
Pattern matched! It's the Album!

00:03:20.708 --> 00:03:24.546
Transmission from Mister Cyril.
Putting it on the monitor.

00:03:24.546 --> 00:03:28.183
Just what is going on here,
Commander Sakaki?!

00:03:28.183 --> 00:03:32.520
Why are the Album and our
Dragon both running wild?!

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:34.622
We are currently investigating that.

00:03:34.622 --> 00:03:38.226
This is an irregular situation,
so details will be forthcoming.

00:03:38.226 --> 00:03:39.853
What?!

00:03:41.696 --> 00:03:43.531
Where are you going, Senpai?!

00:03:43.531 --> 00:03:46.568
Isn't it obvious? To see this with my own eyes!

00:03:46.568 --> 00:03:48.195
Senpai!

00:03:49.537 --> 00:03:52.140
Transmission from Mister Cyril.

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:53.942
Put him through.

00:03:53.942 --> 00:03:56.411
You're aware of the situation, right?

00:03:56.411 --> 00:03:59.747
Request immediate deployment
of the Girouard forces!

00:03:59.747 --> 00:04:03.084
We're already on our way, Mister Cyril.

00:04:03.084 --> 00:04:08.089
I see. Just try to keep the
damage down to a minimum.

00:04:08.089 --> 00:04:09.920
I'll be counting on you.

00:04:11.626 --> 00:04:14.254
All is going according to plan.

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:31.079
That's the Album?

00:04:31.079 --> 00:04:33.445
The third Original, huh?

00:04:51.299 --> 00:04:53.801
Spirytus is settling down.

00:04:53.801 --> 00:04:56.099
The Album is talking to him.

00:05:01.976 --> 00:05:04.479
The Girouard forces?

00:05:04.479 --> 00:05:06.014
Target acquired!

00:05:06.014 --> 00:05:08.778
Now commencing attack.

00:05:22.564 --> 00:05:24.031
Idiot.

00:05:25.033 --> 00:05:26.134
Wait.

00:05:26.134 --> 00:05:29.304
What for?! We have to stop Spirytus!

00:05:29.304 --> 00:05:31.534
We haven't been ordered to.

00:05:46.988 --> 00:05:50.014
This... can't be happening.

00:06:04.239 --> 00:06:05.729
Run!

00:06:25.293 --> 00:06:29.230
It saved Kamishina Jin?

00:06:29.230 --> 00:06:30.754
Toa?

00:06:41.976 --> 00:06:43.603
Stop.

00:06:45.947 --> 00:06:47.574
Stop!

00:06:50.618 --> 00:06:52.882
Stop!!

00:07:12.340 --> 00:07:15.476
The Girouard forces' helicopters
have all been rendered inoperable!

00:07:15.476 --> 00:07:18.413
The Album is moving north,
together with Spirytus.

00:07:18.413 --> 00:07:20.348
They're going to pass over the mainland.

00:07:20.348 --> 00:07:22.441
Commander, what do we do?

00:07:25.086 --> 00:07:28.351
Well, what will you do now, ISDA?

00:07:30.124 --> 00:07:33.025
Your decision, Mister Cyril?

00:07:35.296 --> 00:07:38.493
Our D Project!

00:07:41.969 --> 00:07:45.200
Actualization is authorized.

00:07:51.012 --> 00:07:54.182
That's the Album?

00:07:54.182 --> 00:07:56.484
Actualization approved!

00:07:56.484 --> 00:08:00.011
Lindworm Unit, Actualization approved!

00:08:20.375 --> 00:08:22.009
Spirytus,

00:08:22.009 --> 00:08:24.178
what has come over you?

00:08:24.178 --> 00:08:29.083
We don't have any choice.
We can't just let him go off like this.

00:08:29.083 --> 00:08:31.719
We have to pacify him.

00:08:31.719 --> 00:08:33.550
Howling Star...

00:08:37.892 --> 00:08:39.723
Let's go.

00:08:41.662 --> 00:08:44.222
Incarnate!!

00:08:52.173 --> 00:08:53.731
What?!

00:08:56.077 --> 00:08:57.704
What's that?

00:09:02.183 --> 00:09:05.516
A-A person became a Dragon?

00:09:19.066 --> 00:09:21.899
Howling Star, take off!

00:09:41.489 --> 00:09:43.548
Let's go, Machina!

00:10:16.691 --> 00:10:18.318
Amadeus!

00:10:35.877 --> 00:10:37.868
This can't be...

00:10:39.180 --> 00:10:44.117
A person... riding on a Dragon...

00:11:03.070 --> 00:11:06.641
Our mission is to bring those two
runaway Dragons under control.

00:11:06.641 --> 00:11:09.677
- Got it?
- Roger!

00:11:09.677 --> 00:11:11.304
Acknowledged.

00:11:12.747 --> 00:11:15.383
Urgent transmission from Dr. Kitajima.

00:11:15.383 --> 00:11:17.184
Put it through.

00:11:17.184 --> 00:11:19.854
Commander Sakaki, you promised
me that if you discovered

00:11:19.854 --> 00:11:21.589
either the Album or the Atrum,

00:11:21.589 --> 00:11:24.325
you would secure them
without harming them!

00:11:24.325 --> 00:11:25.860
Secure them without harming them?

00:11:25.860 --> 00:11:28.729
Under the circumstances,
do you think that's possible?

00:11:28.729 --> 00:11:31.599
It's your job to make it possible, right?!

00:11:31.599 --> 00:11:34.001
Are you saying that your
research is more important

00:11:34.001 --> 00:11:37.405
than the safety of the populace?

00:11:37.405 --> 00:11:41.342
I'm not going to let it slide
if you manage to take her life!

00:11:41.342 --> 00:11:45.176
I'll report you to your superiors,
and request a harsh punishment!

00:11:52.053 --> 00:11:54.121
Safety of the populace?
You're the one who wanted

00:11:54.121 --> 00:11:56.555
to use Dragons in actual
combat, aren't you?!

00:12:21.248 --> 00:12:24.118
Yow... What?

00:12:24.118 --> 00:12:25.608
G-10!

00:12:34.829 --> 00:12:37.131
C-Commander Sakaki! It's Gio!

00:12:37.131 --> 00:12:38.758
What?!

00:12:48.442 --> 00:12:50.069
She's calling.

00:13:03.090 --> 00:13:04.819
Caught you!

00:13:06.861 --> 00:13:08.328
Amadeus!

00:13:18.706 --> 00:13:21.004
Everyone, calm down!

00:13:40.361 --> 00:13:42.530
Jin!

00:13:42.530 --> 00:13:45.666
Kazuki? Please!

00:13:45.666 --> 00:13:49.236
You're a Dragonaut, right?
Make them stop, right now!

00:13:49.236 --> 00:13:50.371
Jin...

00:13:50.371 --> 00:13:53.397
That's... that's...

00:13:56.911 --> 00:13:59.146
...that's Toa!

00:13:59.146 --> 00:14:00.511
Jin...

00:14:45.426 --> 00:14:47.053
- T...
- Toa.

00:14:53.801 --> 00:14:55.530
Gio!

00:14:59.373 --> 00:15:02.069
When did you hatch?

00:15:08.783 --> 00:15:11.152
She's calling.

00:15:11.152 --> 00:15:12.642
Toa!

00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:47.478
J-Jin!

00:15:58.666 --> 00:16:00.258
Jin!

00:16:07.041 --> 00:16:08.872
Why?

00:16:11.278 --> 00:16:13.447
Gio belongs...

00:16:13.447 --> 00:16:16.280
...belongs to me...

00:16:19.486 --> 00:16:22.512
Jin!!

00:16:28.529 --> 00:16:29.864
What's that?

00:16:29.864 --> 00:16:35.870
Raina, Gio has run away from
base. He's headed your way.

00:16:35.870 --> 00:16:39.397
I've just sighted him. So that's Gio...

00:16:41.242 --> 00:16:42.176
What's wrong?

00:16:42.176 --> 00:16:44.378
Kamishina Jin is on Gio's back.

00:16:44.378 --> 00:16:45.579
What?!

00:16:45.579 --> 00:16:47.877
They seem to be pursuing the Album.

00:16:53.087 --> 00:16:56.090
Dispatch Spirytus this very instant.

00:16:56.090 --> 00:16:58.592
The Lindworm Unit's
first priority is to secure

00:16:58.592 --> 00:17:01.595
the Album and Kamishina Jin.

00:17:01.595 --> 00:17:02.997
Copy.

00:17:02.997 --> 00:17:05.032
Guys, you heard him.

00:17:05.032 --> 00:17:09.103
We heard him? What does
he mean, dispatch Spirytus?!

00:17:09.103 --> 00:17:10.771
By "dispatch," does he mean?

00:17:10.771 --> 00:17:13.874
Our orders are absolute.

00:17:13.874 --> 00:17:16.076
Howling Star...

00:17:16.076 --> 00:17:18.442
...kill Spirytus.

00:17:20.214 --> 00:17:22.683
- Huh?
- Kill him?

00:17:22.683 --> 00:17:25.552
Didn't you hear me, Howling Star?

00:17:25.552 --> 00:17:28.851
That's an order. Kill Spirytus.

00:18:02.089 --> 00:18:03.784
Nasty...

00:18:07.661 --> 00:18:09.930
Wait, Toa!

00:18:09.930 --> 00:18:13.000
It's me! It's Kamishina Jin!

00:18:13.000 --> 00:18:15.769
You recognize me, right?!

00:18:15.769 --> 00:18:18.169
Why are you leaving?!

00:18:44.631 --> 00:18:46.121
Toa?

00:18:47.968 --> 00:18:50.270
Toa!

00:18:50.270 --> 00:18:52.830
I'm sorry, Jin.

00:18:55.009 --> 00:19:01.215
Now that you've seen my true form,
Jin, I can't stay with you anymore.

00:19:01.215 --> 00:19:03.547
What are you talking about, Toa?

00:19:05.652 --> 00:19:08.712
Farewell, Jin.

00:19:10.391 --> 00:19:12.359
Hold on, Toa!

00:19:19.533 --> 00:19:24.061
Toa, I was born to protect you.

00:19:28.175 --> 00:19:30.677
Let's go, Gio.

00:19:30.677 --> 00:19:35.137
Wait! Toa!!

00:19:49.430 --> 00:19:51.398
Stop!

00:20:25.866 --> 00:20:29.870
You're not alone. I'm here, after all.

00:20:29.870 --> 00:20:31.701
Liar.

00:20:35.209 --> 00:20:38.545
The Album and Gio are both lost.

00:20:38.545 --> 00:20:42.208
Understood. Return to base for now.

00:21:06.440 --> 00:21:08.271
Welcome home.

00:21:23.757 --> 00:21:27.628
As you can see, this is
the site from last night.

00:21:27.628 --> 00:21:32.166
We still do not know any
of the details as of yet,

00:21:32.166 --> 00:21:35.035
but according to eyewitness
reports from local citizens,

00:21:35.035 --> 00:21:36.937
monsters appeared, and...

00:21:36.937 --> 00:21:40.440
We have a follow-up report
on last night's events.

00:21:40.440 --> 00:21:42.442
Apparently, the monsters
that witnesses saw

00:21:42.442 --> 00:21:45.775
have some connection to ISDA...

00:21:54.788 --> 00:22:01.128
"Incoming call"

00:22:07.634 --> 00:22:14.308
The moment our eyes met,

00:22:14.308 --> 00:22:21.081
I felt like the sadness was beginning

00:22:21.081 --> 00:22:27.754
The memories that can't be blotted out

00:22:27.754 --> 00:22:34.990
bind our hearts together, even now

00:22:36.830 --> 00:22:43.670
Though there are as many people

00:22:43.670 --> 00:22:46.673
as there are in these thousands of stars,

00:22:46.673 --> 00:22:50.544
you're the only one that I can see

00:22:50.544 --> 00:22:53.714
Though we may not be able to meet,

00:22:53.714 --> 00:22:56.617
and our wishes might not be granted,

00:22:56.617 --> 00:23:02.923
our growing feelings
are sure to last forever

00:23:02.923 --> 00:23:09.930
If fate tears the two of us apart,

00:23:09.930 --> 00:23:16.770
I believe that just meeting
each other was a miracle

00:23:16.770 --> 00:23:23.377
Look how it flows, like this rain

00:23:23.377 --> 00:23:29.416
I want to let all of my affection fall on you

00:23:29.416 --> 00:23:33.614
Rain of Love

00:23:42.763 --> 00:23:46.967
This is ISDA operator Megumi.
We've finally done it, huh, Ryoko-san?

00:23:46.967 --> 00:23:48.468
We sure have, Megumi-san!

00:23:48.468 --> 00:23:49.603
How did it feel?

00:23:49.603 --> 00:23:53.573
I was so nervous! Dad! Mom! I did it!

00:23:53.573 --> 00:23:57.244
It was tense, huh? I also felt
moved that I finally appeared.

00:23:57.244 --> 00:23:59.479
That makes all three of us, at last.

00:23:59.479 --> 00:24:01.682
Um, don't we have to do
the next episode preview?

00:24:01.682 --> 00:24:03.483
Ah! Is it that late already?!

00:24:03.483 --> 00:24:06.019
Next time, they go out into the
starry sky, and there's big trouble!

00:24:06.019 --> 00:24:07.782
That's it?
